==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|révolter|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|rivoltare|lang=it}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} *{{term||revolvitāre}}, frequentative of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|revolvo|revolvō|roll back|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-revolt.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|əʊlt}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|revolts|revolting|revolted|revolted}}

# To [[rebel]], particularly against authority.
#: ''The farmers had to '''revolt''' against the government to get what they deserved.''
# To greatly [[repel]].
#: ''Your brother '''revolts''' me!''

